  "description": "FRONT AREA\rT1-Southern-blue Gum(Eucalyptus globulis)-small, juvenile\r-section fell to ground level removing\r-use cat scanner to check for utility cabling, dig around stump to ascertain extent of root 'girdling'\r-grind out stump to 350mm below ground \r-back fill hole using grinding arisings, remove excess from site\r\rFRONT AREA\rT2-Mimosa(M.dealbata)\r-reduce crown by 30%(4m max from tips) to suit growth points\r-reduce lateral branch lengths to match with emphasis on front face ensuring good separation from tall street lamp\r-remove extensive deadwood from crown side and any damaged wood\r\rREAR GARDEN\rRear boundary\rT3-Large mature XL Southern-blue Gum(Eucalyptus globulis)\r-reduce crown height by 30%(up to 4.5m) from tallest stems) to suitable growth unions using heavy rigging equipment to safely lower branch sections to ground in a controlled manner \r-reduce lateral branch lengths to match with emphasis on longest inbound facing stems\r-remove any deadwood/damaged branches"
